he same answer. Edges into ","type":"text"},{"code":"root","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and self-loops are never weighed; every other edge is weighed once. ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not kept.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The algorithm is Chu–Liu\/Edmonds with Tarjan’s contraction over mergeable heaps (skew heaps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with lazy offsets) and a union–find with rollback to expand the contracted cycles.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Negative and zero weights are ordinary weights.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"root","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a vertex; every weight is finite (not NaN or infinite); the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differences between weights do not overflow.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","title":"Edges","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Collection","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/Branching":{"url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/branching","title":"Branching","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/